[size=5][b]🔧 Installation[/b][/size]

[size=4][b]Mod Manager[/b][/size]

Install with Thunderstore Mod Manager or r2modman.

This is the easiest option and handles dependencies automatically.

[size=4][b]Manual Installation[/b][/size]

[list=1]
[*]Install [url=https://valheim.thunderstore.io/package/denikson/BepInExPack_Valheim/]BepInExPack Valheim[/url].
[*]Download Recipe Pinner.
[*]Place [font=Courier New]RecipePinner.dll[/font] inside your [font=Courier New]Valheim/BepInEx/plugins/RecipePinner/[/font] folder.
[*]Place the [font=Courier New]RecipePinner_languages[/font] folder next to [font=Courier New]RecipePinner.dll[/font].
[*]Launch the game.
[/list]

Your folder should look like this:

[code]
BepInEx/
└── plugins/
    └── RecipePinner/
        ├── RecipePinner.dll
        └── RecipePinner_languages/
            ├── English.json
            ├── Turkish.json
            └── ...
[/code]

Important: [font=Courier New]RecipePinner_languages[/font] must stay next to [font=Courier New]RecipePinner.dll[/font].

[hr]

[size=5][b]🌍 Languages[/b][/size]

Recipe Pinner auto-detects your Valheim language.

You can also force a language with the [font=Courier New]LanguageOverride[/font] config option.

Version 1.3.0 includes language files for every Valheim-supported language.

Note: Some translations may be imperfect because they were AI-assisted. If you find a bad translation, please report it.

You can also fix one yourself: open the matching [font=Courier New].json[/font] file in [font=Courier New]BepInEx/plugins/RecipePinner/RecipePinner_languages/[/font], edit the text on the right side of each line, and save. Leave placeholders like [font=Courier New]{0}[/font] untouched, since they are replaced with numbers and key names at runtime.

[hr]

[size=5][b]❓ FAQ[/b][/size]

[size=4][b]Does Recipe Pinner craft items automatically?[/b][/size]

No. Recipe Pinner only tracks recipes and materials. You still craft and build normally.

[size=4][b]Does Chest Scanner move items from chests?[/b][/size]

No. It only reads nearby chest contents and includes them in the displayed material counts.

[size=4][b]Is Chest Scanner enabled by default?[/b][/size]

No. Chest Scanner is disabled by default. You can enable it from the config if you want nearby chest contents to count toward requirements.

[size=4][b]Can I pin building pieces?[/b][/size]

Yes. Hammer build pieces can be pinned like crafting recipes.

[size=4][b]What happens if I pin the same recipe again?[/b][/size]

The pin count increases, and the displayed material requirements update for the new count.

[size=4][b]How do I remove or decrease a pin?[/b][/size]

By default, hold [font=Courier New]Left Shift[/font] and press [font=Courier New]Mouse Wheel Click[/font] over the recipe or build piece. You can change the modifier with [font=Courier New]HotkeyUnpin[/font].

[size=4][b]How do I open My Pins?[/b][/size]

Open your inventory and use the My Pins button. From there, you can view, remove, group, disband, and manage pins.

[size=4][b]Can I group pins?[/b][/size]

Yes. Starting with 1.3.0, you can create named Pin Groups from the My Pins panel.

[size=4][b]Can a recipe belong to more than one group?[/b][/size]

Yes. Recipe Pinner supports per-group member claim counts, so duplicate pins can be split between groups or kept as individual pins.

[size=4][b]Can I remove a group without losing the recipes?[/b][/size]

Yes. Use Disband to turn group members back into individual pins.

[size=4][b]Why does my group pin show "+N" instead of all materials?[/b][/size]

Groups with many different materials switch to a compact grid, and that grid is capped so one large group cannot stretch every pin next to it. The materials that do not fit are collapsed into a [font=Courier New]+N[/font] cell.

You can raise the row cap with [font=Courier New]GroupCompactMaxRows[/font], or change when compact mode starts with [font=Courier New]GroupCompactThreshold[/font]. Both apply immediately. A group pinned on its own never shows [font=Courier New]+N[/font].

[size=4][b]Are pins shared between my characters?[/b][/size]

No. Each character has its own pins, saved separately. Switching characters loads that character's own list.

[size=4][b]Does Recipe Pinner work with MyLittleUI?[/b][/size]

Yes. AutoDetect can adjust the HUD layout when MyLittleUI is installed to reduce overlap with other UI elements.

[size=4][b]Can I change the controls?[/b][/size]

Yes. Hotkeys can be changed from the config. Using Configuration Manager is recommended.

[size=4][b]Why did some config settings reset after updating?[/b][/size]

Version 1.3.0 reorganized config categories. If a setting moved to a new category, you may need to review or reapply it.

[size=4][b]Why are some translations imperfect?[/b][/size]

Version 1.3.0 includes language files for every Valheim-supported language, but some translations were AI-assisted. Please report incorrect or awkward translations.

